---
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CallToAction from '../../components/CallToAction.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import amphitheaterHero from '../../assets/communities/maize/clair-donnelly-amphitheater-city-of-maize.jpg';
import amphitheaterWide from '../../assets/communities/maize/clair-donnelly-amphitheater.jpg';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Maize, Kansas Community Guide | Charity Menefee"
  description="A practical introduction to Maize, Kansas, including its northwest Wichita setting, residential growth, local landmarks, and property considerations."
  pageClass="page-interior page-maize"
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Community guide · Maize"
    title="Close to Wichita, with an identity of its own."
    intro="Maize is an independent and growing city on the northwest edge of Wichita, with its own civic identity and close connections to the wider metro."
    image={amphitheaterHero}
    imageAlt="Clair Donnelly Amphitheater and the Maize water tower during an evening community event"
    variant="community"
    imagePosition="center 48%"
    imagePositionMobile="68% center"
  />

  <section class="section-space" aria-labelledby="maize-overview-title">
    <div class="shell editorial-grid">
      <div data-reveal="left">
        <p class="eyebrow">Getting oriented</p>
        <h2 id="maize-overview-title">A separate city that meets northwest Wichita closely.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal="right">
        <p>Maize is an incorporated city on the northwest side of the Wichita metro. K-96 is a useful geographic and access reference for understanding this part of the area, but the municipal boundary isn't always visually obvious from the road.</p>
        <p>In everyday driving, the transition between Maize and northwest Wichita can feel subtle. Roads, neighborhoods, shopping, and other destinations connect the area closely, while Maize still maintains its own city identity and local civic spaces.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-space section-surface" aria-labelledby="maize-housing-title">
    <div class="shell editorial-grid">
      <div data-reveal="left">
        <p class="eyebrow">Housing in a growing city</p>
        <h2 id="maize-housing-title">Residential growth is part of Maize's story.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal="right">
        <p>Newer neighborhoods such as The Coves, The Heights at Maize, Eagle View Estates, and Addis Woods are part of Maize's recent growth. They're useful places to know about when getting familiar with the area, but availability will vary.</p>
        <p>For a particular property, confirm where it sits within that changing map. Review the lot, any covenants or assessments, and how the surrounding streets and infrastructure are actually laid out.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="photo-story section-space section-sage" aria-labelledby="maize-character-title">
    <div class="shell photo-story-grid">
      <div class="photo-story-copy" data-reveal="left">
        <p class="eyebrow">Local character</p>
        <h2 id="maize-character-title">City Park gives Maize a recognizable gathering place.</h2>
        <p>The Clair Donnelly Amphitheater in Maize City Park is used for concerts, performances, and community events. Together with the civic area around Academy Avenue and the Academy Arts District, it provides a visible expression of Maize's identity beyond its residential growth and close geographic connection to Wichita.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="photo-story-main" data-reveal="right">
        <Picture
          src={amphitheaterWide}
          formats={['avif', 'webp']}
          widths={[480, 720, 960, 1280, 1600]}
          sizes="(min-width: 48rem) 62vw, 100vw"
          alt="Clair Donnelly Amphitheater in Maize City Park during an evening performance"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-space" aria-labelledby="maize-practical-title">
    <div class="shell editorial-grid">
      <div data-reveal="left">
        <p class="eyebrow">Practical things to know</p>
        <h2 id="maize-practical-title">The address deserves a closer look.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal="right">
        <p>Because Maize meets northwest Wichita so closely, confirm whether a property is actually inside Maize city limits and which municipal details apply to that address. A familiar road name or a nearby destination doesn't always answer that question.</p>
        <p>It also helps to compare the route from the address to K-96 and northwest Wichita, then review the lot and any development-specific obligations that may affect the property.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-space section-surface" aria-labelledby="maize-search-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading split-heading">
        <div data-reveal="left">
          <p class="eyebrow">Useful questions</p>
          <h2 id="maize-search-title">What should you verify when looking in Maize?</h2>
        </div>
        <p data-reveal="right">These questions help separate broad community context from the details that can vary from one address or development to another.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="question-grid reveal-stagger">
        <li data-reveal="up">Is this property inside Maize city limits, and which municipal services and requirements apply?</li>
        <li data-reveal="up">Is the home in an established area or a newer development, and how does that affect the lot and street pattern?</li>
        <li data-reveal="up">Which access routes would you actually use for work, errands, and other regular destinations?</li>
        <li data-reveal="up">Are there covenants, HOA requirements, special assessments, or other obligations for this address?</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <nav class="shell next-community" aria-label="Community pages">
    <span>Keep exploring</span>
    <a href="/communities/">All communities <i aria-hidden="true">→</i></a>
  </nav>
  <CallToAction
    title="Have questions about a property in Maize?"
    copy="If you're comparing communities or have questions about a specific property, tell me what you're considering. I’ll help you sort through the location and property details that matter."
  />
</BaseLayout>
